content:
I'll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the data files.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Now let me examine the data files to understand their structure and content.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/museum_export_a.csv"
  }
}
```

Let me check the second file as well to see its structure.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/museum_export_b.csv"
  }
}
```

Now I need to see more rows from both files to understand the full dataset. Let me check if there are more rows by using shell commands.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "head -20 data/museum_export_a.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this script to explore the data.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python code/explore_data.py"
  }
}
```

Interesting! Both files only have one row each. This seems like a minimal test dataset. Let me check if there might be more data by examining the files directly with shell commands.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "type data\\museum_export_a.csv"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "type data\\museum_export_b.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this script to perform the analysis.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python code/merge_and_analyze.py"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the improved analysis script.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python code/improved_analysis.py"
  }
}
```

Excellent! The improved analysis successfully merged the duplicate records. Now I need to create the final research report. Let me first check the generated files and then create the report.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Now let me check the generated images to ensure they were created properly.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report\\images"
  }
}
```

Good! Now let me check the deduplicated catalog and summary to include in the report.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "outputs/deduplicated_catalog_final.csv"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "outputs/analysis_summary.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me verify that the report file was created correctly and contains all necessary information.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "report/report.md"
  }
}
```

Perfect! The report has been created successfully with all required components. Let me also verify that the images are properly referenced in the report by checking a few more details.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python -c \"import os; print('Report exists:', os.path.exists('report/report.md')); print('Report size:', os.path.getsize('report/report.md'), 'bytes'); print('Image 1 exists:', os.path.exists('report/images/temporal_analysis_comprehensive.png')); print('Image 2 exists:', os.path.exists('report/images/temporal_distribution.png'))\""
  }
}
```
